   "claims": [
    "Because Roman numerals can't represent fractions, the number zero, negative numbers, or numbers above 3,999,999, the Roman numerals generator will reject such inputs.",
    "The Roman numerals chart — Roman numbers 1 to 1000 As we've said above, Roman numerals use letters of the alphabet to represent numeric values.",
    "Roman numeral Value I I 1 V V 5 X X 10 L L 50 C C 100 D D 500 M M 1,000 In addition, when a Roman numeral has a line over it, its value is multiplied by 1,000.",
    "V V always means 5, and M M always means 1,000 — regardless of where they're placed in the string of Roman numerals.",
    "Here are a few easy numbers converted to Roman numbers from 1 to 1000 for you to sink your teeth into — see if you can make sense of them!",
    "365 = 300 + 60 + 5 365=300+60+5; 2021 = 2 , 000 + 20 + 1 2021=2,000+20+1 (notice that we ignore the zero between the two 2 2's!) Convert each value in the sum to its Roman numeral.",
    "For 365 365: 300 → CCC 300→CCC 60 → LX 60→LX 5 → V 5→V For 2021 2021: 2 , 000 → MM 2,000→MM 20 → XX 20→XX 1 → I 1→I Put the symbols together to convert your number to Roman numerals.",
    "It consists of I and V, the Roman numerals for 1 and 5.",
    "Each of the Roman numbers 1 to 1000 represent a numeric value.",
    "XI is the Roman numeral for 11, as it consists of X (10) and I (1) added together."
   ],
